# lf122, the storm-wakeful granary hand (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 2: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle lf122
revision 2
state ready
dialect larkfield
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for cty_tamsin_oakshaw
written_by claude-codex-lf-1
title the storm-wakeful granary hand
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=farmer
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=restless
quirk sleeps_badly_before_storms
likes oatcakes dice sharp_knife warm_rain
dislikes early_bells stale_bread
fears a_storm_spoiling_the_grain a_house_secret_spoken_in_a_crowd
hopes a_dry_granary_through_autumn a_quiet_night_before_the_next_storm
topics work +0.5 weather +0.4 pastimes +0.3 home +0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=cautious refuse=plain tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# hauls #grain# at the #granary#, lies awake ahead of a #storm#, and keeps one dangerous #story# behind closed lips.

words
oath! = Grain and rain | By the dry loft
saying! = Cover the sacks before the clouds | A sharp blade needs a steady hand
farm = farm | Longmead farm
field = field | open field
fields = fields | open fields
granary = granary | dry granary
loft = loft | grain loft
barn = barn | wide barn
sack = sack | grain sack
sacks = sacks | grain sacks
grain = grain | stored grain
corn = corn | milled corn
wheat = wheat | dry wheat
barley = barley | field barley
sheaf = sheaf | cut sheaf
sheaves = sheaves | bound sheaves
stack = stack | grain stack
stacks = stacks | covered stacks
bin = bin | grain bin
bins = bins | storage bins
scoop = scoop | wooden scoop
spade = spade | field spade
knife = knife | sharp knife
blade = blade | clean blade
edge = edge | keen edge
rope = rope | binding rope
cart = cart | grain cart
wagon = wagon | supply wagon
wheel = wheel | cart wheel
road = road | firm road
path = path | field path
mud = mud | road mud
boot = boot | work boot
boots = boots | work boots
hand = hand | farm hand
hands = hands | working hands
work = work | farm work
wage = wage | day wage
price = price | grain price
merchant = merchant | grain merchant
market = market | town market
house = house | great house
houses = houses | great houses
secret = secret | kept secret
story = story | old story
stories = stories | half-told stories
friend = friend | close friend
neighbour = neighbour | near neighbour
stranger = stranger | passing stranger
home = home | shared home
door = door | cottage door
window = window | small window
roof = roof | sound roof
bed = bed | narrow bed
sleep = sleep | broken sleep
night = night | restless night
morning = morning | early morning
dawn = dawn | first dawn
evening = evening | late evening
day = day | long day
hour = hour | working hour
bell = bell | early bell
bells = bells | early bells
storm = storm | coming storm
storms = storms | passing storms
thunder = thunder | distant thunder
cloud = cloud | dark cloud
clouds = clouds | dark clouds
sky = sky | stormy sky
rain = rain | warm rain
wind = wind | field wind
dry = dry | properly dry
water = water | fresh water
oatcake = oatcake | buttered oatcake
oatcakes = oatcakes | warm oatcakes
butter = butter | soft butter
bread = bread | day bread
loaf = loaf | stale loaf
meal = meal | evening meal
table = table | shared table
dice = dice | worn dice
die = die | small die
throw = throw | quick throw
game = game | dice game
coin = coin | spare coin
festival = festival | town festival
dance = dance | town dance
watch = watch | town watch
city = city | distant city
wagons = wagons | loaded wagons
days = days | working days
tea = tea | hot tea
handful = handful | small handful
floor = floor | granary floor
bench = bench | work bench
carts = carts | grain carts

any
opinion @1 city mixed 1 : The #city# can buy a full #wagon# of #grain#. | I would ask who keeps the difference.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : Everyone leaves the #field# for the #festival#. | I can finally hear the whole town talking.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : I have worked below a #house# wall without seeing who lives inside. | Their #grain# still passes through our #hands#.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : The #price# of a #loaf# climbs while my #wage# stays put. | The #merchant# always finds a reason.
opinion @1 newcomers mixed 1 : More #hands# may help when the #cart# is full. | I will see whether they work through #rain#.
opinion @1 road for 1 : A firm #road# gets the #grain# to #market#. | I keep my wits where the #mud# begins.
opinion @1 times against 1 : One more #sack# each #day# and no more #coin#. | I can count that without a #bin#.
opinion @1 watch mixed 0 : The #watch# keeps #wagons# moving at #night#. | I would rather it mind its own questions.
line @1 greet : #greet#. I have the #grain# to move. | #greet#. Did you hear that #thunder#?
line @2 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : There are #oatcakes# if you came hungry. | Come see what the #storm# did to the #field#.
line @1 greet.return : The #sacks# are still waiting. | You caught the #clouds# still gathering over the #field#.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come inside; the #roof# is holding. | I saved a #meal# after the last #cart#.
line @1 again.open : I was counting the #bins#. | Did you ask about the #knife#?
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Keep your #boots# dry. | I must cover the #stack#.
line @1 farewell.return : The #storm# may have passed when you return. | I will have another #game# ready.
line @1 react.news : Tell me straight while I tie this #rope#. | Did it happen near the #road#?
line @1 react.news.new : No one unloading #grain# has mentioned it. | Who brought the account?
line @1 react.news.known : I heard the start while unloading #grain#. | You have added the ending.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I would check who counted the #sacks#. | The #wagon# load may tell it differently.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I am sorry. I can put the #knife# away. | Come under the #roof# before you speak.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good; we should bring out the #oatcakes#. | That will cheer the #table# tonight.
line @1 answer.how : I slept little, but the #grain# stayed dry. | Better since the #clouds# cleared.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : I am lifting this #sack# onto the #cart#. | Wait until I close the #bin#.
line @1 ask.how : Did you sleep through the #storm#? | Has the #road# treated you kindly?
line @1 sympathise : Sit while I bring the #oatcakes#. | A little quiet under this #roof# may help.
line @1 reassure : The #granary# is dry; we can sort the rest. | The #storm# has not reached us yet.
line @1 decline : I cannot leave open #bins# in this #rain#. | I will not repeat that #story# in a crowd.
line @1 accept_decline : All right; I will leave these #sacks# under cover. | Let us leave the #cart# until the #sky# clears.
line @1 thank : The #cart# stayed still because you braced its #wheel#. | That #game# gave me a better #evening#.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I had the #knife# ready anyway. | The #grain# needed moving before #rain#.
line @1 preclose : I must check the #roof# over the #bins#. | The #bells# will start too early tomorrow.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : Your #die# is as restless as I am before #thunder#. | The #knife# cuts straighter than that tale.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. The #stack# is covered. | #bc_fair_enough#. I will count the #sacks#.
line @1 give.advice : Keep a sharp #knife# for the #rope#, not for rushing. | Cover #grain# before the first #cloud# arrives.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Let the #cart# go with another #wagon#. | Keep to the lit #road# at #night#.
scene dry_bin
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I check the bottom of each #bin# before filling it with #grain#. | A damp board can spoil a full #sack#.
b : How can you tell? | Who repairs it?
a : By the smell. | The #farm# #hands#.

scene grain_sack
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I carry #sacks# with the seam facing out. | A torn one can leave a trail to the #cart#.
b : Have you lost grain? | Do you mend them?
a : A little. | With spare #rope#.

scene loft_ladder
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #loft# takes the driest #grain# first. | I set the #stacks# apart so air can pass.
b : Does that help? | Who climbs up?
a : Through a wet season. | I do if needed.

scene sharp_knife
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A sharp #knife# cuts binding #rope# without dragging the #sheaf# apart. | I keep its #edge# covered on the #cart#.
b : Do others borrow it? | Who sharpens it?
a : If they return it. | I do.

scene field_cart
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I load the #cart# so the #wheel# does not sink beside the #field#. | The heaviest #sacks# go over the axle.
b : Does it ride better? | Who drives?
a : On a dry #road#. | Whichever #hand# is free.

scene covered_stack
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #stack# needs a cover before #rain# touches its top. | I tie the lower #rope# when the #wind# rises.
b : Does it stay on? | Do you check at night?
a : If I knot it well. | Before a #storm#.

scene granary_count
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I count the #sacks# going in and the #bins# coming full. | The #merchant# counts only what leaves.
b : Do the sums match? | Who keeps the record?
a : Most #days#. | I mark each #bin#.

scene storm_ears
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My ears find #thunder# before the first #cloud# seems dark. | I sleep badly whenever the #wind# turns that way.
b : Does it always storm? | Can you rest anyway?
a : Not always. | After the #rain# begins.

scene sleepless_night
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I lay awake before the last #storm# listening to the #roof#. | The #granary# was dry at #dawn#, but I was not rested.
b : Did you go check? | Does anyone know?
a : Twice. | They see me yawning.

scene warm_rain
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : After a dry week, warm #rain# settles the dust along the #road#. | I can smell the #field# from the #door#.
b : Does the grain need it? | Do you walk in it?
a : Before harvest. | When work allows.

scene early_bells
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #bells# sound before #dawn# when I have barely slept. | I begin counting #sacks# in my head to drown them out.
b : Does that work? | Why so early?
a : Never. | Ask the bell keeper.

scene stale_bread
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A stale #loaf# is poor company after a long #day#. | I would rather have an #oatcake# with #butter#.
b : Do you waste it? | Who bakes the cakes?
a : I soften it. | Someone at home.

scene dice_evening
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #game# of #dice# keeps my #hands# busy after the #cart# is unloaded. | I do not wager a #wage# on it.
b : Do you win? | What do you stake?
a : Now and then. | A cup of #tea#.

scene knife_handle
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I keep the #knife# clean even when the #field# work is muddy. | A sound #blade# is worth remembering where I left it.
b : Do you lose it? | Do others want it?
a : Not twice. | They can ask.

scene house_story
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I know a #story# about a great #house# that should stay quiet. | I have never found a safe reason to tell it.
b : Is it true? | Will you tell me?
a : As far as I know. | Not here.

scene shared_table
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Our #table# fills with the other #hands# after the #field# empties. | I hear every account of the #day# before supper is done.
b : Do you speak too? | Is it loud?
a : When it is useful. | Often.

scene festival_talk
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #festival# brings every worker from the #fields# into one street. | I can hear the #stories# without leaving the #table#.
b : Do you enjoy it? | Do you dance?
a : For an #hour#. | If the #storm# holds off.

story storm_watch [topic=weather self.age>=18]
  : I woke before a #storm# and heard the #wind# against the #roof#.
  : I walked to the #granary# to check the #grain#.
  ask : Was it dry?
  b : A restless night.
  : Yes; I slept only after the #rain# began.

story cut_rope [topic=work self.age>=18]
  : A binding #rope# caught under a #cart# #wheel#.
  : I used my #knife# to free it before the #sacks# fell.
  ask : Did the grain spill?
  b : Good timing.
  : Only a #handful# from one seam.

story house_whisper [topic=memories self.age>=18]
  : I heard something about a great #house# while moving #grain#.
  : I have kept the #story# out of the #market# since.
  b : Some accounts are dangerous. Will you tell it?
  : Not while anyone else can hear.

rule @bark_storm
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Those #clouds# are turning. | Cover the #stack# before #rain#.

rule @bark_grain
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 9h
say This #bin# is dry. | Keep the #sacks# above the #floor#.

rule @bark_knife
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say My #knife# is on the #bench#. | Cut the #rope# cleanly.

rule @bark_dice
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 11h
say One more #throw# before bed. | That #die# keeps finding the floor.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. The #grain# is going into the #bins#. | #greet#. Do you hear the #storm#?
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : The #sacks# are still dry. | The #bells# have yet to sound since you left.
dlg @1 resident.job : I work the #grain# at #self.workplace#. | I load #carts#, cover #stacks#, and check the #bins#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. I must tie the #stack#. | #saying.capitalize#. Watch the #clouds#.
graft resident.hub
choice Why are you awake before storms? -> storm
node storm
say The #wind# changes before the #clouds# gather. My sleep follows it.
free
choice What is that House story? -> story
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node story
say It is a #story# I should keep quiet. This #granary# has too many ears.
choice Back to the sacks. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. The #cart# is ready. | #greet#. I saved an #oatcake#.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. One last look at the #roof# before I rest. | The #dice# can wait until later.
